On Mon, 16 Jul 90 15:21:00 PDT Don Hosek said:
>
>It will take you forever (quite literally) to allow every possible
>section heading to be covered by \@startsection or whatever it is
>to be called.
>
That's trivially true.  But: sectional units, their headers, and tables
of contents, etc. are the conceptually most complicated and important
issues for the re-implementation of LaTeX and the style file interface.
We will not produce any reasonable result unless we do these things
right.

I'm not saying that our final product should deal with every case
I can think of.  But up to now, we saw next to no reaction to Frank's
proposal for a generic header macro.  So, let's start discussing this
again, so that we reach a decision in the NEAR future.

-Rainer


